updated_at: "2026-08-18T06:50:14.394Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-18T06:45:51.710Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-18T06:45:51.710Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: The package manifest exposes the exact recovery command named by the calibration gate and it forwards update arguments correctly; A negative control removes or renames the script and proves gate recovery conformance fails; Testing documentation and the gate error use one executable spelling
parent: pm-mpbb
resolution: Context intent calibration now names a manifest-backed executable recovery command and the repository assurance gate fails when that reference is missing or renamed.
expected_result: "The calibration contract points operators and agents to a command that exists in the package manifest, runs successfully, and is protected by a negative control."
actual_result: "context:intent:calibrate is declared and executable; the focused 11-test suite, aggregate assurance, packed acceptance, and exact full coverage pass."
